  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1100 PM MDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nA pattern shift is underway. The Four Corners high has weakened \nwith a new center over TX. This is turning flow from east to west \nto south to north. Moistening is underway as well, and we saw an \nincrease in thunderstorm coverage as a result though it had \nresulted in a lot of dust thanks to high temperature - dewpoint \nspreads. We will remain in this southerly flow through early next \nweek, which will give us daily shower and thunderstorm chances. \nWith PW values ranging between 1.25-1.5\", heavy rainfall and flash\nflooding will be the main concern. These rainfall chances will \nespecially be enhanced with the passage of any short-wave troughs.\nThe GFS and Euro continue to show a notable trough/low passing \nthrough the area Saturday into Sunday. With the increased \nmoisture, highs will be closer to normal. We will see at least a \nbreak from the 100 degree temperatures. \n\nThe forecast for next week is a bit uncertain. The GFS and Euro \nshow the high pushing back to the west though there has been poor \nrun-to-run consistency how far west it shifts and how much dry air\nshifts in with it. A look at the LREF though does show a distinct\ndownward turn in moisture.",
